WEBVTT

01:44.813 --> 01:47.357
You may be the strongest in the USA

01:48.525 --> 01:51.277
but you're a convict, my friend.

01:51.945 --> 01:54.781
You've been given way too much space.

01:55.365 --> 01:58.868
This is only one fifth of what I've got.

02:00.328 --> 02:02.789
Loaded with an excessive amount of muscle.

02:03.414 --> 02:07.794
A book collection the size of a library.
You still have as much as you had before.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.882
It looks to me like a sign of insecurity.

02:14.634 --> 02:17.470
That son of yours, Baki,

02:18.054 --> 02:20.765
I heard he fought that ancient man.

02:21.891 --> 02:24.310
What do you think of the result?

02:24.894 --> 02:30.066
A man who was born weak fought
a genuinely strong man into a corner

02:30.150 --> 02:34.070
and ultimately forced him
to use a weapon, namely martial arts.

02:34.654 --> 02:37.657
Therefore, the weak man won.

02:38.741 --> 02:40.076
<i>How incredibly impure.</i>

02:42.871 --> 02:44.205
<i>How incredibly filthy.</i>

02:44.706 --> 02:46.332
<i>How incredibly muddled.</i>

02:46.916 --> 02:48.334
<i>How incredibly frivolous.</i>

02:49.127 --> 02:51.588
<i>Emotion. Effort. Diligence.</i>

02:52.130 --> 02:56.342
<i>Such decorations
often tarnish a pure fight.</i>

02:57.760 --> 03:01.598
<i>They complicate
the simple fruit that is victory.</i>

03:04.642 --> 03:07.353
I'm at a disadvantage in a fist fight.

03:09.647 --> 03:12.066
At the moment a fight is decided,

03:12.150 --> 03:15.904
whoever's head is positioned
at the highest elevation above sea level...

03:16.905 --> 03:18.323
is the victor!

03:20.241 --> 03:26.206
<i>At this moment, Biscuit Oliva's head
was 1,105.8 meters above sea level,</i>

03:26.748 --> 03:31.669
<i>while Yujiro Hanma's head
was 1,106.3 meters above sea level.</i>

03:32.545 --> 03:35.840
I figured this would happen.

03:39.928 --> 03:42.347
You are looking very healthy, sir.

03:42.430 --> 03:43.264
RESILIENCE

03:43.348 --> 03:44.933
I am pleased to see it.

03:45.934 --> 03:47.894
Quit being so formal.

03:47.977 --> 03:49.854
Let me see your face.

03:51.147 --> 03:53.358
PRIME MINISTER

03:53.441 --> 03:56.152
It hasn't been long
since you assumed office.

03:56.236 --> 03:58.363
You must have much to be concerned about.

03:59.155 --> 04:02.867
The responsibility is heavy,
and at times, I regret it.

04:08.081 --> 04:10.124
- So now, my man...
- Yes?

04:10.792 --> 04:13.503
This weight that is causing you trouble,

04:13.586 --> 04:15.880
how many kilos do you need to lighten it?

04:16.673 --> 04:18.633
"Kilos," sir?

04:19.300 --> 04:21.135
So naive.

04:21.970 --> 04:24.555
Money, my man,

04:25.765 --> 04:29.727
it is not counted in yen, but in kilos.

04:30.228 --> 04:32.647
In kilos?

04:36.234 --> 04:38.653
10,000 YEN

04:39.237 --> 04:41.239
I have prepared 300 kilos.

04:41.322 --> 04:44.659
When converted to yen,
that's more than three billion.

04:45.243 --> 04:47.662
Take it with you in a truck.

04:49.122 --> 04:50.164
Huh?

04:50.790 --> 04:54.544
Prime Minister,
trusting that you are a real man,

04:54.627 --> 04:56.921
I have a favor to ask you.

04:59.090 --> 05:00.425
I am at your service.

05:00.508 --> 05:02.927
MINISTRY OF EDUCATION
AGENCY FOR CULTURAL AFFAIRS

05:03.511 --> 05:04.762
This is incomprehensible.

05:04.846 --> 05:08.599
This is merely a fight
between a father and son,

05:08.683 --> 05:10.685
but he wants the country's tacit approval?

05:10.768 --> 05:12.020
MINISTER OF DEFENSE

05:12.103 --> 05:16.649
Well, since this is something
that I must know due to my position,

05:16.733 --> 05:21.195
the previous Minister of Defense
informed me of the existence of this man.

05:21.279 --> 05:22.655
"Due to your position"?

05:23.197 --> 05:26.284
You mean you knew of Yujiro Hanma?

05:27.118 --> 05:29.203
Who exactly is this man?

05:30.788 --> 05:34.709
Well, I'm not quite sure how to explain.

05:35.460 --> 05:38.046
Let's just say that he's mighty.

05:38.755 --> 05:41.424
He's strong, extraordinarily so.

05:41.507 --> 05:43.343
"Strong," you say?

05:43.426 --> 05:44.886
In brute strength.

05:44.969 --> 05:46.971
Let's call it, "physical strength."

05:47.055 --> 05:51.059
Huh? Do you mean this
when you say "brute strength"?

05:51.559 --> 05:54.312
Yes, that's right.
That kind of brute strength.

05:55.605 --> 05:59.484
This is making even less sense. Japan
is a country governed by laws, you know.

06:00.151 --> 06:02.445
No matter how much
brute strength this man has,

06:02.528 --> 06:05.948
once the police get involved,
that would be the end of it, right?

06:06.032 --> 06:07.700
No, that would not be the end of it.

06:07.784 --> 06:09.577
Huh? What do you mean by that?

06:10.912 --> 06:14.290
<i>The Prime Minister
a few administrations ago</i>

06:14.374 --> 06:17.168
<i>was assaulted by Yujiro Hanma
in their official residence.</i>

06:17.251 --> 06:18.836
<i>In the official residence?</i>

06:18.920 --> 06:22.006
<i>Where were the security guards?
Did he sneak in?</i>

06:22.090 --> 06:26.010
<i>Since Yujiro Hanma had declared
he would attack ahead of time,</i>

06:26.094 --> 06:30.515
<i>there were no less than
100 fully-equipped riot police on duty.</i>

06:31.224 --> 06:32.767
Okay. And?

06:33.643 --> 06:36.604
He smashed right through them with ease.

06:37.105 --> 06:40.024
Don't be ridiculous!
What sort of sorcery is that?!

06:40.608 --> 06:43.027
Did you know about this too,
Minister of Education?

06:43.111 --> 06:44.028
MINISTER OF EDUCATION

06:44.112 --> 06:46.030
I had only heard rumors.

06:46.114 --> 06:51.160
That Prime Minister placed a gag order
on the incident, to maintain public order.

06:51.244 --> 06:52.745
Maintain public order?

06:52.829 --> 06:54.038
- Minister...
- Yes?

06:54.705 --> 06:56.749
<i>The brute strength of a single man</i>

06:56.833 --> 07:00.044
<i>successfully attacked
the linchpin of the nation.</i>

07:00.711 --> 07:05.550
As the head of our educational system,
Minister, I would like your opinion.

07:06.467 --> 07:08.511
It is completely unacceptable.

07:09.637 --> 07:14.559
It could have an immeasurably
bad influence on young men.

07:15.268 --> 07:16.644
I see.

07:16.727 --> 07:19.689
It could definitely lead
to the praising of violence.

07:20.189 --> 07:23.568
But even so, Minister of Defense,

07:24.152 --> 07:28.072
doesn't the nation have weapons,
the most powerful brute strength?

07:28.906 --> 07:32.452
Prime Minister, let me tell you
a very simple truth

07:32.535 --> 07:36.080
that will help
in understanding Yujiro Hanma.

07:38.666 --> 07:43.087
<i>The United States of America has,
with Yujiro Hanma alone, formed a...</i>

07:43.713 --> 07:46.507
<i>A treaty of friendship?!</i>

07:54.140 --> 07:55.349
This is the man.

07:55.975 --> 07:59.187
This is the most recent image
of Yujiro Hanma, a.k.a. Ogre,

07:59.270 --> 08:01.689
that I personally possess.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.275
SECRETARY-GENERAL
OF THE DEMOCRATIC PEOPLE'S PARTY

08:04.358 --> 08:07.612
The image taken last year of the man
known as the strongest being on Earth.

08:07.695 --> 08:11.574
That's quite a face.
It's almost demon-like.

08:11.657 --> 08:13.367
It is not just demon-like.

08:13.951 --> 08:16.120
He truly is a demon.

08:18.206 --> 08:20.791
Don't tell me that you are a fan of his.

08:22.251 --> 08:26.380
It appears that you do not understand,
so allow me to explain.

08:27.089 --> 08:31.844
The man Yujiro Hanma is the only man
in this world who is a brute strength pro.

08:32.553 --> 08:34.055
"Brute strength"?

08:34.597 --> 08:37.892
With one of his powerful arms,
he can make anything happen.

08:38.476 --> 08:40.895
He is the aspiration of all men.

08:41.646 --> 08:43.814
What the Minister of Defense said

08:43.898 --> 08:47.985
about the treaty of friendship
between him and the U.S. is all true.

08:48.069 --> 08:50.905
About that... what about a sniper?

08:51.489 --> 08:55.409
If shot at with a rifle from long range,
he could be killed, right?

08:55.993 --> 08:56.994
Impossible.

08:57.495 --> 09:01.958
Since he has a treaty of friendship with
the U.S., they would become our enemy.

09:02.041 --> 09:06.420
Then it must be possible
for the U.S. to kill him with a sniper.

09:06.504 --> 09:07.880
That won't happen either.

09:07.964 --> 09:11.551
Because the whole world
desires to join forces with Ogre.

09:13.010 --> 09:14.470
- Prime Minister.
- Yes?

09:14.554 --> 09:18.933
Right now, Yujiro Hanma is
the most powerful weapon in the world.

09:19.016 --> 09:24.397
Making him an ally is the only way
to be victorious over major nation states.

09:24.480 --> 09:26.315
Since that's how important he is,

09:26.399 --> 09:29.902
who in the world, that is to say,
what country would ever try to kill him?

09:30.486 --> 09:34.156
Earlier, you asked if I was a fan
of Ogre, Prime Minister.

09:34.240 --> 09:35.408
It seems to me you are.

09:35.992 --> 09:37.910
Whether it were a member of parliament,

09:37.994 --> 09:43.916
or a manga artist, or a pianist,
or a rock musician, or a soldier,

09:44.000 --> 09:47.920
if any of them had been born
with the brute strength of Yujiro,

09:48.504 --> 09:51.424
they all would have used their strength
to achieve their dreams.

09:51.507 --> 09:54.218
They all would have
chosen the path of Ogre.

09:55.011 --> 09:57.930
In other words, everyone,
including us politicians,

09:58.014 --> 10:01.934
use our occupation as a
substitute for brute strength?

10:02.893 --> 10:06.814
That is why he is the only
brute strength pro in the world.

10:11.819 --> 10:18.200
I repeat, what you will be taught here
is not for improving your character

10:18.784 --> 10:21.704
nor for defending yourself
against unjust violence.

10:22.288 --> 10:23.956
It is straight-up violence,

10:24.457 --> 10:27.793
that is to say, techniques
that are used on the battlefield.

10:28.419 --> 10:30.713
Therefore, there is no such thing
as foul play.

10:30.796 --> 10:34.842
Or rather, if something is foul play,
then use it immediately.

10:35.718 --> 10:37.970
I have read about your pasts.

10:38.721 --> 10:39.555
Mark, stand up.

10:43.059 --> 10:45.561
You've been a Muay Thai fighter
for a long time.

10:45.645 --> 10:50.066
You're also a mixed martial arts fighter
and have even fought in pro boxing rings.

10:52.193 --> 10:55.488
This is an order. Kill me in a free fight.

10:58.240 --> 10:59.241
Yes, sir.

11:15.758 --> 11:17.093
Howard, your turn.

11:18.886 --> 11:22.139
<i>Judo fighter, Howard: eyes poked out.</i>

11:23.224 --> 11:26.769
<i>Boxer, Richard: over-the-head throw.</i>

11:27.770 --> 11:31.399
<i>Wrestler, Schmidt: struck down.</i>

11:32.525 --> 11:36.153
<i>Old-style</i> kobujutsu <i>fighter, Takahashi:
tightly bound.</i>

11:37.363 --> 11:40.950
There's a difference between
civilian and battlefield martial arts.

11:41.033 --> 11:44.412
I'm sure even you dunces now have
a small understanding of what that is.

11:44.995 --> 11:46.789
Commit yourselves to using foul play.

11:46.872 --> 11:49.417
That is the orthodox style
of battlefield fighting.

11:49.500 --> 11:50.334
That is all.

11:52.044 --> 11:52.962
Dismissed!

11:53.045 --> 11:54.004
Yes, sir!

12:06.100 --> 12:07.059
<i>My friend.</i>

12:07.935 --> 12:10.062
<i>I've made you wait a long time.</i>

12:15.151 --> 12:17.153
<i>Now, I am finally...</i>

12:19.697 --> 12:20.990
<i>prepared.</i>

12:22.533 --> 12:27.163
<i>Now, I'm confident I won't disappoint you.</i>

12:28.164 --> 12:30.583
<i>For this day, for this night...</i>

12:31.208 --> 12:32.585
<i>I have long waited.</i>

12:33.169 --> 12:34.587
<i>Just you wait...</i>

12:36.172 --> 12:38.674
<i>my friend, Yujiro Hanma.</i>

12:40.342 --> 12:44.680
<i>Being the strongest isn't something
you become. It is something that you are.</i>

12:45.181 --> 12:49.518
<i>To say you're seeking or aiming for it
is admitting that you've not achieved it.</i>

12:50.352 --> 12:54.774
<i>Strydum, if you want
to maintain our relationship,</i>

12:54.857 --> 12:57.276
<i>then once a year, you must try to kill me.</i>

12:58.360 --> 13:02.114
<i>It does not matter if you do it
fairly or not, just threaten my life.</i>

13:02.865 --> 13:04.533
<i>Knives are okay.</i>

13:04.617 --> 13:06.368
<i>Guns are okay.</i>

13:06.452 --> 13:08.120
<i>Explosives are okay.</i>

13:08.204 --> 13:09.872
<i>Nuclear weapons are okay.</i>

13:11.624 --> 13:14.084
<i>Devote your body and mind to the task.</i>

13:14.835 --> 13:17.755
<i>Have the determination
to finish me off at all costs.</i>

13:18.464 --> 13:21.592
<i>If you wish to be known
as an acquaintance of Yujiro Hanma,</i>

13:22.468 --> 13:25.387
<i>if you want to be recognized
as someone close to Ogre,</i>

13:26.472 --> 13:29.141
<i>then that is the only way to achieve it.</i>

13:30.059 --> 13:33.687
<i>Strydum, devise a plan
with the intentions of killing me.</i>

13:34.730 --> 13:35.564
Hey.

13:44.073 --> 13:47.243
Yujiro, this time...

13:55.918 --> 13:58.838
This time it's what?

13:58.921 --> 14:01.966
Never mind. You don't have to tell me.

14:03.425 --> 14:05.845
Last year, you said it was
"once-in-a-century."

14:05.928 --> 14:08.347
Two years ago,
it was "an unparalleled sight."

14:08.430 --> 14:10.850
Before that, it was
"the greatest the world has..."

14:12.101 --> 14:15.604
Those are like catchphrases
for selling Beaujolais nouveau.

14:25.447 --> 14:29.368
Strydum, you've broken your promise.

14:31.579 --> 14:34.874
You face me already having given up,
thinking you couldn't possibly win!

14:35.916 --> 14:36.876
No...

14:36.959 --> 14:39.879
<i>These fists I've embedded with gunpowder</i>

14:40.462 --> 14:42.882
<i>and these boot tips
I've embedded with gunpowder...</i>

14:43.465 --> 14:45.426
<i>If only I could land just one strike!</i>

14:47.970 --> 14:50.472
Though you are Ogre,
you were still born human.

14:50.556 --> 14:53.475
It's unlike you to misread me,
Yujiro Hanma.

15:06.363 --> 15:09.742
What's this about misreading you?

15:11.076 --> 15:15.748
Ogre, what an outrageous misunderstanding.

15:16.874 --> 15:18.834
I hadn't given up yet.

15:19.335 --> 15:20.419
I have...

15:21.670 --> 15:23.589
<i>only given up just now.</i>

15:23.672 --> 15:25.299
That's hot!

15:34.433 --> 15:35.267
<i>I waited.</i>

15:36.393 --> 15:37.728
<i>I simply waited.</i>

15:38.479 --> 15:41.231
<i>In the back of the dim room, at the wall,</i>

15:41.982 --> 15:45.819
<i>where it shouldn't even exist, I've waited
for the moment when it would appear.</i>

15:46.820 --> 15:48.238
<i>Without stirring an inch.</i>

15:49.615 --> 15:50.741
<i>In a cascade of sweat.</i>

15:52.409 --> 15:53.243
<i>Here it comes!</i>

15:54.286 --> 15:56.246
<i>See? See?</i>

15:56.997 --> 15:57.831
<i>It's here!</i>

16:06.006 --> 16:07.257
<i>No good.</i>

16:07.341 --> 16:09.593
<i>That's no good. It needs more.</i>

16:14.974 --> 16:18.060
<i>Even stronger, even faster,</i>

16:18.143 --> 16:21.355
<i>even more frightening, even more cunning.</i>

16:22.439 --> 16:24.358
<i>This ain't good enough!</i>

16:35.869 --> 16:37.871
- What? An earthquake?!
<i>-</i> Turn on the TV!

16:37.955 --> 16:39.790
- It's here!
<i>-</i> Seismic intensity of three?!

16:59.184 --> 17:02.312
<i>Even greater than I imagined.</i>

17:02.396 --> 17:04.565
Huh? What?

17:05.149 --> 17:06.734
There's no need to be surprised.

17:07.234 --> 17:10.571
I was just wondering if you'd been
getting proper medical checkups.

17:11.155 --> 17:12.823
Medical checkups?

17:14.158 --> 17:18.579
Yujiro, are you concerned about my health?

17:18.662 --> 17:22.082
Don't be stupid.
I'm just keeping up the small talk.

17:27.171 --> 17:29.590
My, you certainly are kind.

17:29.673 --> 17:31.842
From your own child
to the national government,

17:31.925 --> 17:37.097
even as far as the military, you treat
them all with utterly zero distinction.

17:37.181 --> 17:39.767
If anyone were to get in your way,

17:39.850 --> 17:44.521
whether it be an infant or the military,
you'd treat them mercilessly.

17:44.605 --> 17:46.190
I get it. Fine.

17:46.690 --> 17:48.817
That's exactly why you're "Ogre"!

17:48.901 --> 17:51.361
That is you, isn't it, Yujiro Hanma?

17:52.988 --> 17:54.823
But then there you go...

17:54.907 --> 17:57.951
Worrying about
the health of this old dotard.

18:02.664 --> 18:06.460
Yujiro, have you gone senile?

18:07.961 --> 18:08.879
Old man...

18:09.379 --> 18:10.881
What a letdown.

18:11.715 --> 18:13.092
That's enough of that.

18:14.468 --> 18:16.428
You've ruined my mood, Yujiro.

18:18.806 --> 18:19.890
Didn't you hear me?

18:20.474 --> 18:23.102
You better believe I can, you idiot!

18:23.185 --> 18:26.897
Don't you even realize
what the hell you just said?

18:27.481 --> 18:30.484
Yujiro Hanma, of all people!

18:49.753 --> 18:51.463
I warned you.

18:56.510 --> 18:57.594
Get a doctor.

18:58.762 --> 19:00.681
Noble Elder!

19:02.766 --> 19:04.268
<i>Is it fortune or misfortune?</i>

19:05.269 --> 19:08.355
<i>This man who has specialized
so much in fighting,</i>

19:08.438 --> 19:13.193
<i>before he knew it,
he'd obtained a special power.</i>

19:14.486 --> 19:17.698
<i>The ability to identify the weak points
of everyone within his sight.</i>

19:17.781 --> 19:21.034
<i>From the most infinitesimal cancer cells
that they haven't even noticed,</i>

19:21.118 --> 19:22.953
<i>to the undiscovered tooth cavity.</i>

19:23.954 --> 19:28.083
<i>All these weaknesses
spring to his notice as sensitive points.</i>

19:29.251 --> 19:31.461
<i>Once, it was well-honed fists...</i>

19:32.296 --> 19:34.631
<i>Once, it was perfectly sharpened swords...</i>

19:35.883 --> 19:37.885
<i>Once, it was flying bullets...</i>

19:39.136 --> 19:40.929
<i>Eventually, it was modern weapons...</i>

19:42.097 --> 19:45.434
<i>He smashed, crushed, and overcame them.</i>

19:46.018 --> 19:48.854
<i>He destroyed, insulted
and laughed at them.</i>

19:49.605 --> 19:53.150
<i>He didn't have a single failure
in his life as a brute strength pro.</i>

19:55.110 --> 19:59.448
<i>More than a precisely-crafted stethoscope...</i>

20:00.282 --> 20:02.284
<i>More than
a high-performance x-ray machine...</i>

20:03.076 --> 20:05.370
<i>More than a highly-experienced surgeon</i>

20:05.454 --> 20:07.789
<i>or the most capable
eastern medicine specialist...</i>

20:07.873 --> 20:09.374
<i>This man's history equipped him</i>

20:09.458 --> 20:12.961
<i>with the ability to identify weakness
that far outperformed them all.</i>

20:13.462 --> 20:15.255
<i>Is it fortune or misfortune?</i>

20:17.966 --> 20:19.927
CENTER BOXING GYM

20:21.845 --> 20:22.679
Huh?

20:27.351 --> 20:28.185
Yes?

20:31.521 --> 20:32.648
Here for a tour?

20:32.731 --> 20:33.690
No.

20:34.733 --> 20:36.693
I would like approval to join.

20:36.777 --> 20:39.905
Huh? "Approval"?

20:40.614 --> 20:43.450
As long as you pay the registration fee,
anyone can join.

20:44.576 --> 20:45.953
But, ya know...

20:46.578 --> 20:49.957
I can see that my lack
of a foot bothers you.

20:50.040 --> 20:54.044
Well, if you're doing it to stay healthy,
that kind of thing is fine.

20:54.544 --> 20:58.215
Naturally, I would like instruction
to become a fighter.

20:59.800 --> 21:02.886
There's no way, pal. Not with that leg.

21:02.970 --> 21:04.221
Who would it trouble?

21:05.013 --> 21:09.977
Who exactly would be inconvenienced
by the fact that I lack one foot?

21:12.562 --> 21:14.398
Take off your shoe and get in here.

21:14.982 --> 21:16.483
I appreciate this.

21:19.069 --> 21:20.904
Smack this thing.

21:20.988 --> 21:22.030
"Smack"?

21:22.614 --> 21:24.992
I mean punch it with all your might.

21:25.575 --> 21:28.745
<i>He wants me to punch
this fragile thing with all my might?</i>

21:30.622 --> 21:33.292
Um, do you have a replacement ready?

21:33.375 --> 21:35.752
Huh? Aw, come on, pal!

21:35.836 --> 21:38.338
If you smash this bag to pieces,

21:38.422 --> 21:41.008
then I'll be your exclusive coach, pal.

21:41.883 --> 21:43.010
Gladly.

21:43.093 --> 21:46.221
Please, do not forget your words.

21:47.931 --> 21:51.727
<i>I'm pretty confident I can gain
approval to join without destroying this,</i>

21:51.810 --> 21:53.270
<i>but I'll still...</i>

21:54.938 --> 21:55.772
<i>give them a show!</i>

22:08.618 --> 22:10.537
What?

22:11.413 --> 22:14.124
Coach, sign me up.

22:16.126 --> 22:17.377
He's awesome...
